    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "At noon, the Tongxin Cafeteria in Shanghai’s Jing’an District is crowded, and Chen Luo is waiting in line. She lives alone and works at a nearby office building. “Preparing my own meals takes too much time,” she said. “I used to spend two hours "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " but only ten minutes eating.” For a long time, she depended heavily on food deliveries. Her parents always "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the safety of those meals."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The Tongxin Cafeteria is a perfect solution for Chen. It’s one of the city’s more than 1,600 "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "community",
            "ref": "v-community"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " canteens. They were built to provide quick, healthy meals at fair prices for "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Therefore, they were known as “senior canteens” at first. Now, however, these canteens are becoming "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " with young people as well. Many of them share their dining "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " on social media. As a result, more people have started showing up at community canteens."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Some young people still hesitate. That’s not because they have doubts about the quality of food, though. Instead, they’re worried about "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the seniors’ places. “They don’t need to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". We serve elderly diners from 10:30 to 11:30 a.m. and 4:30 to 5:30 p.m.,” said Li Jiajun, the manager of a local community canteen. “Apart from those "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", people of all ages are welcome.” Another staff worker, surnamed Yu, "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". “With more young diners, we have better "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "profits",
            "ref": "v-profit"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ",” he said. “This gives us more confidence to keep the canteen open for a long time.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Young people are also warmly "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " by the seniors. “We’re happy to have them dining here,” said a 90-year-old. “They give an ‘elderly canteen’ a feeling of youth.”"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
